Subject: [PATCH] Use the typed SDK DSL for Molly's NetCipher module

AGP 9.4 rejects the numeric SDK catalog string passed to compileSdkVersion.
Match Signal's compileSdk release DSL while retaining the pinned SDK version
and strict dependency verification.

Carry this AI-assisted source change as its own
reviewable patch, preserving the original source author and diff.
The official Molly snapshot and earlier resolution patches do
not receive regenerated provenance headers.

Source-Commit: 2dafc7253c580f9d63236ced700f49ef40d93997
AI-Generated: true

diff --git a/lib/netcipher/build.gradle b/lib/netcipher/build.gradle
index b02e0547eb16781ceb010201394304060b7731ac..6609ddbb6c3b1cf95df87894ed29d241e156b38e 100644
--- a/lib/netcipher/build.gradle
+++ b/lib/netcipher/build.gradle
@@ -6,7 +6,9 @@ android {
     namespace 'info.guardianproject.netcipher'
 
     buildToolsVersion = libs.versions.buildTools.get()
-    compileSdkVersion = libs.versions.compileSdk.get()
+    compileSdk {
+        version = release(libs.versions.compileSdk.get().toInteger())
+    }
 
     defaultConfig {
         minSdk = libs.versions.minSdk.get().toInteger()
